    {
      "id": "0ngjzZ68I1nl10I2Y99r-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 165.83536895623524,
      "y": 9932.781692694787,
      "width": 2700,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1722541989,
      "version": 60,
      "versionNonce": 150833483,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779289733793,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What a Snowflake ID Consists Of :- \n\nA standard Snowflake ID is a 64-bit signed integer split into four distinct structural parts: \n\n   1 bit      41 bits (Timestamp)        10 bits (Machine ID / Worker ID)    12 bits (Sequence)\n┌───┬─────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────┬──────────────┐\n│ 0        │ 011010110...0101                │   0000101011                           │ 000000000101 │\n└───┴─────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────┴──────────────┘",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What a Snowflake ID Consists Of :- \n\nA standard Snowflake ID is a 64-bit signed integer split into four distinct structural parts: \n\n   1 bit      41 bits (Timestamp)        10 bits (Machine ID / Worker ID)    12 bits (Sequence)\n┌───┬─────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────┬──────────────┐\n│ 0        │ 011010110...0101                │   0000101011                           │ 000000000101 │\n└───┴─────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────┴──────────────┘",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wnatk7kl4_JSKzVancLw0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 149.5067840483348,
      "y": 10289.126863958565,
      "width": 9.39599609375,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 663039627,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1403865035,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779288107763,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "sAznji5dl-XxHTGvDo3MP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 174.74608451358358,
      "y": 10295.96057609776,
      "width": 2620.8349609375,
      "height": 1260,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 513783723,
      "version": 1266,
      "versionNonce": 1825466469,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779289713024,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n-> 1st bit is for SIGN 0 means always +ve,  \n\n-> Next 41 bits are epoch time,  \n\n-> Next 10 bits, here is Zookeeper plays key role whenever server signup or registers zookeper assign a unique code to that server and it stores in persisted Node\nso whenever sever restarts too same id assigned. Here maximum value is (0 to 1023) that means maximum 1024 servers we can registers to zookeeper at a time.\n\n-> Last 12 bits are local counter value which we maintain at zookeeper. From 0 to 4096\n\n\nNote:- Multiple requests come, 2 servers receive request at a same time then timestamp might be same. In this secnario surely workerId / machineID would be \ndifferent.\n\n\nTotal comes around 64 bit characters. If you convert this Interger Base10 format value would be huge 19-digit decimal number (e.g., 1541815603606036480).\n\n\nNow to get Random 6~7 digit characters we perform Base62 operation on this snowflake id\n\n\nBase2 ==> 0,1\nBase10 ==> 0-9\nBase62 ==> a-zA-Z0-9\nBase64 ==>  a-zA-Z0-9+- (Plus and minus are extra chracters here)\nBase128 , Base256 ... ===> Here all other special chracters, emojies ASCII values would come in to picture.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n-> 1st bit is for SIGN 0 means always +ve,  \n\n-> Next 41 bits are epoch time,  \n\n-> Next 10 bits, here is Zookeeper plays key role whenever server signup or registers zookeper assign a unique code to that server and it stores in persisted Node\nso whenever sever restarts too same id assigned. Here maximum value is (0 to 1023) that means maximum 1024 servers we can registers to zookeeper at a time.\n\n-> Last 12 bits are local counter value which we maintain at zookeeper. From 0 to 4096\n\n\nNote:- Multiple requests come, 2 servers receive request at a same time then timestamp might be same. In this secnario surely workerId / machineID would be \ndifferent.\n\n\nTotal comes around 64 bit characters. If you convert this Interger Base10 format value would be huge 19-digit decimal number (e.g., 1541815603606036480).\n\n\nNow to get Random 6~7 digit characters we perform Base62 operation on this snowflake id\n\n\nBase2 ==> 0,1\nBase10 ==> 0-9\nBase62 ==> a-zA-Z0-9\nBase64 ==>  a-zA-Z0-9+- (Plus and minus are extra chracters here)\nBase128 , Base256 ... ===> Here all other special chracters, emojies ASCII values would come in to picture.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
